  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "PGA2040 is an 8x8 pin-grid with a double perimeter ring (48 positions). Transcribed from the left view (with the RP2 chip) as displayed; the right view is its mirror. The grid was split into four 2-row connectors: top and bottom take full 8-column double rows (corners included), left and right take the remaining rows 3-6. Numeric labels are GPIO numbers as printed. GND positions are drawn as white circles with a bar (legend 'GND'). Group tags UART (GPIO0/1), ADC (26-29 shaded) and GPIO are colour categories and were not added as functions."
